Common unchecked exceptions

NullPointerException
	indicated a null reference

IndexOutOfBoundsException
	indicates that an index (e.g., an index for an array) is outside the appropriate range

ArithmeticException
	indicates the occurrence of an exceptional arithmetic condition (e.g., integer division by zero)

IOError
	indicates the failure of an I/O operation

ClassCastException
	indicated an invalid attempt to cast an object to type of which the object is not an instance (e.g., casting a Double to a String)
	
IllegalArgumentException
	indicated an illegal or inappropriate method argument

